DexSwapModuleIntegration
├── full lifecycle
│   ├── it should swap tokens end-to-end via PaymentRails → Module → Router
│   ├── it should emit ActionExecuted from PaymentRails with correct amountOut
│   ├── it should emit SwapExecuted from Module
│   ├── it should revoke module approval after successful swap
│   └── it should allow any address to execute (permissionless)
├── router revert
│   ├── it should return false from PaymentRails.executeAction
│   ├── it should revoke PaymentRails→Module approval
│   └── it should preserve paymentRails token balance
├── slippage revert
│   ├── it should return false from PaymentRails.executeAction (caught by try-catch)
│   ├── it should revoke PaymentRails→Module approval
│   └── it should preserve paymentRails token balance (atomic rollback)
├── validation failures at PaymentRails level
│   ├── it should revert when amount is below minBalance
│   ├── it should revert when amount exceeds balance
│   ├── it should revert when token is not enabled
│   └── it should revert when amount is zero
├── validation failures at module level
│   ├── it should return false when router is not whitelisted
│   └── it should return false when target token equals sell token
├── consecutive executions
│   └── it should succeed on multiple swaps draining the paymentRails
├── preview execution
│   └── it should return (0, targetToken) since atomic swaps cannot pre-estimate
├── executeAction with executionData overload
│   └── it should forward executionData to module and execute swap
├── multi-paymentRails — shared module
│   ├── it should swap from two paymentRails sharing one module
│   ├── it should handle interleaved executions from multiple paymentRails
│   └── it should fail both paymentRails when router is removed
├── router whitelist changes
│   ├── it should use newly added router on next execution
│   └── it should fail execution when router is removed between configure and execute
├── module ownership — integration
│   ├── it should allow new owner to manage routers after transfer
│   ├── it should block old owner after transfer
│   └── it should keep existing router whitelist after ownership transfer
└── paymentRails reconfiguration
    ├── it should work after disable then re-enable
    └── it should work after swapping to a new module
